# 3.13 and not the newest CPython, and the reason is a comparand rather
# than a preference: coincurve, one of the wrappers
# scripts/01-libsecp256k1.py exists to compare, publishes wheels up to
# cp313 and no further, and its sdist does not build at all: its build
# hook looks for cffi's LICENSE at the root of cffi's .dist-info, and the
# cffi its build resolves keeps it under licenses/. A benchmark that
# cannot install its comparands measures nothing -- and the
# documentation build
# holds the same pin for a different reason: .readthedocs.yaml and
# docs.yml both install that wrapper through the uniform install
# command btclib-org/.github's reusable-docs.yml runs for every
# repository, though no page imports it (btclib-org/.github#35).
# secp256k1 publishes wheels up to cp313 too, but its sdist needs no
# system pkg-config, pkgconf being a build dependency in pyproject.toml's
# [tool.uv] (issue #427). On macOS it also holds the pin, having no
# arm64 wheel past cp313 and a build that can fail in an automake rebuild
# (issue #244).
# The other two wrappers hold no part of this: btclib_secp256k1 publishes
# past cp313, and electrum-ecc builds a py3-none wheel, reaching the C
# through ctypes rather than linking it into an extension.
# Raise this the moment coincurve installs on the newer CPython, and
# on macOS secp256k1 does too (issue #381);
# requires-python in pyproject.toml stays at its own floor either way,
# which secp256k1lab sets at 3.11. .readthedocs.yaml's own copy of this
# pin moves with it: Read the Docs cannot read this file directly.
3.13
